abstract: >-
  A theory of the selected higher-star defect Delta(D) = H_k / im_Z(A) of a
  t-design incidence lattice: a sandwich bound and finiteness, a pointed
  presentation with a parameter-only Gram/discriminant envelope, a prime-by-prime
  analysis of the discriminant form (good-prime decomposition, an odd
  valuation-one Witt obstruction strict on an infinite S(2,5,v) family, an
  exceptional-prime rank-three reduction, and a binary higher-valuation
  metabolicity theorem), fixed-parameter phenomena (a valuation-two formula, a
  same-parameter separation of two STS(15), the complete STS(15) spectrum), a
  Pasch transport law, an elementary realization theorem, and geometric
  applications. Classical ingredients are attributed; no priority or firstness is
  claimed. The self-contained finite controls are reproduced by an included
  script.
